ser.py", "canonical VKX reader, written against the published format spec"], ["race_legs.py", "finds the real race start; first upwind and downwind from GPS alone"], ["race_multi_leg.py", "multi-leg segmentation by track reversal; duration, distance, SOG, VMG proxy"], ["start_line.py", "line geometry from the VKX line-position rows"], ["wind_grib.py", "ICON-EU and ECMWF GRIB decoding"], ["fetch_wind.py", "builds data/wind.json; called every 3 h by GitHub Actions"]], "automation": [["GitHub Actions", "every 3 h on GitHub servers; commits data/wind.json only when the forecast moves"], ["Scheduled task", "every 3 h locally; re-checks race reports, results and new logs. Needs the desktop app open"]]}, "brief": {"start": ["Distance to gun", "Time to gun", "Speed at gun", "Angle at gun"], "leg": ["Boat speed", "Boat VMG — most important", "Tacks / gybes", "Tack loss per tack", "Gybe loss per gybe", "Best moments", "Worst moments", "Places gained / lost per leg"], "race": ["Boat position against wind shifts", "Choice of downwind mark, left or right", "Official start list and results", "Course and mark GPS, rounding positions"], "done": ["VKX decoding — all 25 logs parse byte-exact to EOF", "Start-line geometry — line length agrees with the event reports to within 3 m", "Model bias recalibrated across three races — +19.1, +18.0, +11.2, mean +16.1, with a light-air guard", "Wind outlook to Friday, three-model consensus, refreshed every three hours", "Race start resolved — anchor on the LAST timer event, not the first", "Boat identity resolved — Team Sweden is the vakaros logs, confirmed by byte-size match", "Official finishing positions pulled from cncascais.com — Team Sweden (SWE 1121 Garm, Per Roman) finished 16th, 57th and 10th, 83 net points, 23rd overall after 3 races", "Start-line bias validated three times — pin favoured in every race, and our formula reproduces the event's own 107 m / 206 m / 137 m within 2% each time", "8 September telemetry expanded from 14 boats to 30 — near-complete against the event's 34-boat analysis set, so fleet-relative figures are now a real fleet comparison"], "open": ["9 September has telemetry for only 3 boats (J70 Let it be, Mag, Yupi) — and Team Sweden's own log for today is not among them, so there is no analysis of the team's racing today", "Race 4 (9 Sep) is scored on cncascais.com — Garm 48th in-race, 27th overall on 131 pts — but has no ib-sailing wind/bias analysis and no synced team telemetry yet, so it isn't in the race explorer or the bias calibration table.", "Wind-referenced VMG per leg. race_multi_leg reports a straight-line proxy, not VMG. The function already takes a wind_deg argument and the measured per-leg winds are known, so this is plumbing, not new machinery", "Best and worst moments, and places gained or lost per leg — both follow from real VMG", "Race 3 (8 Sep) is analysed only from the event report — no leg tables here, because none of the 34 boats' race-3 telemetry has been decoded yet", "Official results are known per race now (3 races scored), but not yet joined boat-by-boat to the telemetry — the race explorer's order column is still last-rounding position, not the finish", "Course and mark GPS — marks are inferred from track reversals, so extra-distance carries unknown error", "Heel and pitch — the orientation quaternion is present and clean, never converted"]}, "coach": {"source": "Team coach, 9 Sep 2026, with an annotated replay of race 1 (wind label 317°T)", "mechanism": "The breeze bends against the shoreline. That is what makes the right side mostly the stronger one — and it is the same bend that puts the GRIB 11-19° to the right of reality, because a 7 km grid cell cannot resolve it.", "start": [["Right is stronger, but do not pay for it", "Never sacrifice 100–200 m of line bias to get there. A committee-boat start cannot win that back."], ["If you can see bias, take it", "If the bias is visible at all it is probably big enough to be worth more than anything else available on the first beat."], ["The pin is a long way from the course", "The top mark sat above the RC boat, so the pin was about 1 km across the course axis. Starting there only works if you can go right almost immediately."], ["Nothing on the beat gives it back", "What is lost at the gun stays lost. Spend the pre-start gathering clues, not settling."]], "gate": "Gate bias mattered as much as the line. With the left shift at the bottom of the course, the right-hand gate turn came out considerably further upwind.", "topmark": "A gybe set was the right call — but not from the front pack, where the offset boats throw a lot of dirty air. Spread fleet and more breeze makes it easy; compact fleet and less breeze makes the wind shadow big enough to change the answer.", "between": "Sail between races. Check wind direction, line bias and top-mark position every time. The biggest decision of the next race is made before the gun, not after it."}, "official": {"source": "cncascais.com official results (live scored)", "updated": "09/09/2026 20:33 local", "races_scored": 4, "top": [{"pos": 1, "sail": "ESP 1283", "boat": "Marnatura", "pts": 20}, {"pos": 2, "sail": "BRA 641", "boat": "Oceanpact - Viking", "pts": 31}, {"pos": 3, "sail": "BRA 1795", "boat": "Areté", "pts": 38}, {"pos": 4, "sail": "POR 284", "boat": "Navis Portugal", "pts": 44}, {"pos": 5, "sail": "POR 1282", "boat": "Another Affair", "pts": 46}], "team": {"pos": 27, "sail": "SWE 1121", "boat": "Garm", "skipper": "Per Roman", "r1": 16, "r2": 57, "r3": 10, "r4": 48, "pts": 131}, "fleet_scored": 100, "drive_new": ["Nautique J70 (BRA — Nautique) 9-8-2026.vkx", "Aretê 1872 (BRA 1795 — Areté) 08-09-2026.vkx", "To Nessa 1527 (BRA 1527 — To Nessa) 08-09-2026.vkx"], "race4_note": "Race 4 sailed and scored today (9 Sep); no ib-sailing wind/bias report published for it yet, and no team telemetry (vkx) for 9 Sep has synced to Drive or Downloads, so it cannot be added to the race-explorer or the bias calibration table this ru